      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(config): use JSON5.stringify with JSON5-comment-loss warning on config write",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw uses JSON5 to parse user configurations (supporting comments and trailing commas), but writes them back with standard JSON.stringify which strips all user-authored comments, explanations, and structure definitions on every automatic config write.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. Use JSON5.stringify instead of JSON.stringify for the output format. JSON5.stringify produces valid JSON5 with unquoted keys and trailing commas, matching the parse-side expectations and reducing formatting churn.\n\n2. Add a warning when the original config contains JSON5 comments (// or /*) that will be lost through the parse-modify-stringify roundtrip. The warning fires once per config path when comments are detected in the raw source.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Reduces unnecessary formatting churn (unquoted keys preserved, trailing commas kept)\n- Users are now warned when their JSON5 comments will be stripped\n- Config file remains valid JSON5, so future comments can be added back\n- No change to config semantics or parsing\n\n## Evidence\n\n```\n$ node -e \"const j5 = require('json5'); const o = {a:1,b:'hello'}; console.log(j5.stringify(o, null, 2));\"\n{\n  a: 1,\n  b: 'hello',\n}\n```\n\n### Tests\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/config/schema.test.ts\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  59 passed (59)\n\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/config/io.owner-display-secret.test.ts\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  2 passed (2)\n```\n\n### Lint + format\n```\n$ npx oxlint -c .oxlintrc.json src/config/io.ts  # No errors\n$ npx oxfmt --check src/config/io.ts              # All matched files use the correct format\n```\n\n## What Changed\n\n- src/config/io.ts: +17/-1 (JSON5.stringify + comment-loss warning)\n\nFixes #105683\n\n## AI Assistance\n- AI-assisted: Yes\n- Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n- Human confirmed understanding: Yes",
